    "title": "pandas.DatetimeIndex.timetz — pandas 2.2.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.DatetimeIndex.timetz#\n\n- \n*property* DatetimeIndex.timetz[source]#\n- Returns numpy array of `datetime.time` objects with timezones.The time part of the Timestamps. Examples For Series: >>> s = pd.Series([\"1/1/2020 10:00:00+00:00\", \"2/1/2020 11:00:00+00:00\"]) >>> s = pd.to_datetime(s) >>> s 0 2020-01-01 10:00:00+00:00 1 2020-02-01 11:00:00+00:00 dtype: datetime64[ns, UTC] >>> s.dt.timetz 0 10:00:00+00:00 1 11:00:00+00:00 dtype: object For DatetimeIndex: >>> idx = pd.DatetimeIndex([\"1/1/2020 10:00:00+00:00\", ... \"2/1/2020 11:00:00+00:00\"]) >>> idx.timetz array([datetime.time(10, 0, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), datetime.time(11, 0, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)], dtype=object)",
    "markdown_length": 693,
